-- int-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT TO FAIL.  Each puts to the integrated row the answer of a reading it did not take, as if
-- that were the answer; each fails exactly where the two readings part.  Their number is the `expected_failed` of this file in
-- check.sh and `expected_red` in encoding.json.  A refusal would not do here (a refused assertion is not a failed one), so each is
-- chosen to be answered, not refused, by the integrated row.

§ `Tests that fail on purpose: the readings the integrated row did not take`

`red: a 5 kW system` MEANS `fixture: a system of` 5 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"
`red: Noa with a grade 1 licence` MEANS `fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Noa, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2029 2 1)
`red: Dana with a grade 1 licence` MEANS `fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2025 12 1)
`red: the engagement of Noa for oil in maintenance` MEANS `fixture: the engagement by` `fixture: Ofek Ltd, a corporation` `of a person holding` (LIST `red: Noa with a grade 1 licence`) `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `for work on the system` `red: a 5 kW system` `amounting to` `B.3(3) adding or replacing oil during maintenance`
`red: Dana's lapsed work` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `red: Dana with a grade 1 licence`) `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`

-- RED 1.  The PLAN's integration point IP3 wired group 3's s.18(a) from the capacity alone: the operator may engage a grade 1 holder to add oil in maintenance on 5 kW.  The row wires it from the kinds appropriate to the work (First Schedule column A), as s.3(a) reads "appropriate": the answer is no.
#ASSERT `int — the operator may engage the person in` `red: the engagement of Noa for oil in maintenance`

-- RED 2.  Reading: the Registrar's duty to grant did not exist before the commencement day (a gate that answers no).  The row answers by a refusal before that day, and group 2's ungated function says yes.
#ASSERT NOT `int (with no commencement gate) — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` (`fixture: an application by` (`fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` `fixture: Dana, an individual`) `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2025 7 15)) `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 0)

-- RED 3.  Group 1's fork F8, the alternative: a licence that is not in force still counts as a licence held, so lapsed work is item (2).  The row's default is "no licence at all".
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `red: Dana's lapsed work` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work`

-- RED 4.  Reading: "the programme was approved" is satisfied by a programme that needs no consent (group 4's other function).  The row takes the stricter: no consent given, not approved.
`red: a short course that leads to no final certificate and has no consent` MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` WITH
    `the programme` IS "short course"
    `a final certificate as stated in section 6(a)(4) can be obtained through the programme` IS FALSE
    `the Registrar consented to the programme` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar approved the programme in` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` (`fixture: an application by` (`fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` `fixture: Dana, an individual`) `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1)) `with the programme being` (JUST `red: a short course that leads to no final certificate and has no consent`) `and the amount paid being` 284)

-- RED 5.  Group 7's fork F-E-1, reading (a): s.58 is a wide gateway, so electrical work outside the integral electrical system is open to the licensee.  Wired to group 1's definition of "work on a cooling system" that work is not work at all, so the answer is no.
`red: electrical work outside the integral system` MEANS `fixture: limits of the item set in the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `red: Dana with a grade 1 licence`) `on` (YMD 2025 12 2) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(12) electrical work in the integral electrical system only`) `to` `fixture: facts with neither limit satisfied`
#ASSERT `int — the licensee of the situation is treated as a service electrician` `red: electrical work outside the integral system`

-- RED 6.  A sanction with no earlier violation priced as a repeat violation (twice the updated amount).
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for` (`int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` `red: Dana's lapsed work` `with the reference` "red-6") `priced from` (`fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` (YMD 2030 6 15)) `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `the sanction is` 40800

-- RED 7.  The Second Schedule's three years counted from the later commencement of paragraph (2) of s.63(a) (16.1.2027, so to 16.1.2030): the experience item would still be open on 17.7.2028.  The row counts them from the commencement day of paragraph (1) as the Law's note says, so it is closed.
`red: an applicant with the year 2027 of work` MEANS `fixture: an applicant with only the periods of work, being` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `and the periods` (LIST (`Period of work on cooling systems` WITH `first day of the period` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `last day of the period` IS YMD 2027 12 31))
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) (`int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `red: an applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17)))

-- RED 8.  Regulation 3 not applied: the licence fee on 5.5.2026 under the amended text is still the printed 284.
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees` EQUALS JUST 284

-- RED 9.  The PLAN counted five heads of fee in s.59; group 7 counts six and the row follows group 7.
#ASSERT count (`s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`) EQUALS 5

-- RED 10.  Group 5's fork F-OFFENCE, the alternative: a conviction for a disciplinary offence that the Minister finds unfit bars an inspector.  Group 5 takes "offence" as criminal; the integrated row follows group 5.
`red: a candidate inspector with only a disciplinary conviction` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` WITH
    `an employee of the Ministry` IS TRUE
    `record of offences` IS `Record of offences` WITH `convicted of a criminal offence` IS FALSE, `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS TRUE, `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS FALSE, `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS FALSE
    `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` IS TRUE
    `received the training the Minister directed in the field of the powers he will hold` IS TRUE
    `meets the further conditions of eligibility, if the Minister directed any` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `red: a candidate inspector with only a disciplinary conviction`

-- RED 11.  Group 2's fork FV4, the alternative: a licence is valid from the day AFTER the grant.  The row follows group 2's default: in force on the grant day.
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `red: Dana with a grade 1 licence` (YMD 2025 12 1)

-- RED 12.  The last year of validity of a one-year licence starting on the day it was granted (the first day of the licence belonging to its last year).  Group 3 counts the last year back from the last day and leaves out the anniversary: the grant day is outside it.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1)

-- RED 13.  Group 1's fork F1, the alternative: "up to 70 kW" excludes 70, so a 70 kW system is beyond grade 2.  Groups 1 and 2 both take the limit as inside.
#ASSERT NOT elem `grade 2 licence` (`licence kinds that cover a cooling system` (`fixture: a system of` 70 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"))

-- RED 14.  A subcommittee's delegated advice sufficing for an exemption order (function (1)): group 4 allows delegation only for function (3).
#ASSERT `int — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order after` (`int — a consultation on an exemption whose advice came from` (`a subcommittee that advises the Council` WITH `the Council delegated its powers in the function to the subcommittee` IS TRUE, `the subcommittee proceeded as the procedure fixed by the Council requires` IS JUST TRUE)) `with the Minister's satisfaction being` TRUE
